      78/       0 :                     ; *** ZERO PAGE SUBROUTINES ***
      79/       0 :                     ;
      80/       0 :                     ; THE 8080 INSTRUCTION SET LETS YOU HAVE 8 ROUTINES IN LOW
      81/       0 :                     ; MEMORY THAT MAY BE CALLED BY RST N, N BEING 0 THROUGH 7.
      82/       0 :                     ; THIS IS A ONE BYTE INSTRUCTION AND HAS THE SAME POWER AS
      83/       0 :                     ; THE THREE BYTE INSTRUCTION CALL LLHH.  TINY BASIC WILL
      84/       0 :                     ; USE RST 0 AS START AND RST 1 THROUGH RST 7 FOR
      85/       0 :                     ; THE SEVEN MOST FREQUENTLY USED SUBROUTINES.
      86/       0 :                     ; TWO OTHER SUBROUTINES (CRLF AND TSTNUM) ARE ALSO IN THIS
      87/       0 :                     ; SECTION.  THEY CAN BE REACHED ONLY BY 3-BYTE CALLS.
      88/       0 :                     ; BY USING RST CALLS, ROM CODE IS REDUCED BY ABOUT 200 BYTES.
      89/       0 :                     ;
      90/       0 :                             ORG  0H
