    2205/     AF3 :                     ;*************************************************************
    2206/     AF3 :                     ;
    2207/     AF3 :                     ; *** TABLES *** DIRECT *** & EXEC ***
    2208/     AF3 :                     ;
    2209/     AF3 :                     ; THIS SECTION OF THE CODE TESTS A STRING AGAINST A TABLE.
    2210/     AF3 :                     ; WHEN A MATCH IS FOUND, CONTROL IS TRANSFERED TO THE SECTION
    2211/     AF3 :                     ; OF CODE ACCORDING TO THE TABLE.
    2212/     AF3 :                     ;
    2213/     AF3 :                     ; AT 'EXEC', DE SHOULD POINT TO THE STRING AND HL SHOULD POINT
    2214/     AF3 :                     ; TO THE TABLE-1.  AT 'DIRECT', DE SHOULD POINT TO THE STRING.
    2215/     AF3 :                     ; HL WILL BE SET UP TO POINT TO TAB1-1, WHICH IS THE TABLE OF
    2216/     AF3 :                     ; ALL DIRECT AND STATEMENT COMMANDS.
    2217/     AF3 :                     ;
    2218/     AF3 :                     ; THE TABLE CONSISTS OF ANY NUMBER OF ITEMS.  EACH ITEM
    2219/     AF3 :                     ; IS A STRING OF CHARACTERS WITH BIT 7 SET TO 0 AND
    2220/     AF3 :                     ; A JUMP ADDRESS STORED HI-LOW WITH BIT 7 OF THE HIGH
    2221/     AF3 :                     ; BYTE SET TO 1.
    2222/     AF3 :                     ;
    2223/     AF3 :                     ; END OF TABLE IS AN ITEM WITH A JUMP ADDRESS ONLY.  IF THE
    2224/     AF3 :                     ; STRING DOES NOT MATCH ANY OF THE OTHER ITEMS, IT WILL
    2225/     AF3 :                     ; MATCH THIS NULL ITEM AS DEFAULT.
    2226/     AF3 :                     ;
